## 1. Project Title & One-Paragraph Problem Statement

**Title:** Sunlight & Shadow Analyzer (SSA): an interactive sun-path, shadow and sunlight-hours tool for small-site planning.

**Problem statement:** The stakeholder is a junior urban planner or architecture student working on small urban plots in a dense city such as Lahore. This is an assumed persona for the course. Her pain point is that she cannot quickly see how a proposed building changes sunlight on neighbouring courtyards, rooftops and gardens over a whole day. Professional tools (Ecotect, SketchUp plugins, GIS suites) are heavy, licensed or online-only. Hand-drawn shadow diagrams show only one or two instants, so a layout's worst hours are easy to miss. **Solution:** a fully offline Python/tkinter app where she drags simple box buildings onto a ground plane, scrubs a time/date slider to watch the sun and shadows move in real time, runs a sunlight-hours heatmap, and compares two layouts (before/after) with numeric and visual differences. Every assumption and uncertainty is disclosed in the interface.

