## 2. Success Criteria

Each criterion is testable via Help → "Run self-tests", Help → "Benchmark", or the manual checklist in §10.

- **SC1 Solar accuracy.** For the four reference cases in §10 (three daytime, one night) the computed azimuth and elevation fall within the stated tolerances (azimuth ±2° to ±4°, elevation ±1°). The self-test shows 100 % pass.
- **SC2 Shadow direction and length.** For Lahore (31.5204° N, 74.3587° E, UTC+5) on 2024-03-21 at 10:00 local:
  - sun azimuth is 129° ± 2° and elevation is 46.3° ± 1.5°;
  - the ground shadow of a 10 m tall wall points along bearing 309° ± 2°;
  - its length is 9.6 m ± 0.6 m (L = H / tan(elevation)).
- **SC3 Responsiveness.** With 15 buildings and the 30×30 grid, dragging the time slider across its full range (or dragging a building) gives p95 redraw time ≤ 66 ms (≥ 15 FPS). This is measured by the built-in benchmark over 100 redraws.
- **SC4 Task time.** In a 5-person pilot, at least 4 of 5 first-time users can add a building and state its shadow direction within 30 s. At least 4 of 5 can drag a building to a new cell within 5 s.
- **SC5 Heatmap speed and UI liveness.** With defaults (15 buildings, 15-min step, full day), "Run heatmap" finishes in ≤ 5 s in pure Python. The progress bar updates ≥ 5 times per second, no UI freeze exceeds 200 ms, and Cancel takes effect within 0.5 s.
- **SC6 Heatmap correctness.** For an unoccluded ground cell, hours equal the independent 1-minute-scan reference within ±0.25 h (≈ 11.8 h for Lahore, 21 March, elevation threshold 2°). A cell 2 m north of the centre of a 20 m-wide, 30 m-tall wall on 2024-12-21 shows 0.0 h.
- **SC7 Comparison integrity.** The displayed Δ total equals an independently computed Σ(B−A) over common free cells within 1e-6 h. Toggling comparison on and off 20 times in a row causes no exception and each toggle takes ≤ 1 s. After any edit, the "stale" indicator appears within 100 ms.
- **SC8 Disclosure and accessibility.**
  - The Assumptions dialog is reachable in ≤ 2 clicks and lists ≥ 6 assumptions.
  - Legend swatch colours exactly equal rendered heatmap cell colours for every bin (automated check).
  - All text/background pairs meet WCAG contrast ≥ 4.5:1 (computed in the self-test from palette constants).
  - Every heatmap value is readable as a number via hover, so colour is not the sole channel.
  - Every control is reachable by Tab, and a selected building can be moved by arrow keys alone.

